WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.410 --> 00:00:01.410
Okay.

00:00:01.410 --> 00:00:02.410
I want your help with something.

00:00:02.410 --> 00:00:07.210
Um, this actually does not have anything to
do with the youtube issues that we're experiencing.

00:00:07.210 --> 00:00:11.180
Every once in a while I just like to reflect
on the format of the show and think about

00:00:11.180 --> 00:00:13.880
what changes we might be able to make to improve
the show.

00:00:13.880 --> 00:00:21.160
Uh, based on changing, uh, demands, changing
interests from the audience and the different

00:00:21.160 --> 00:00:24.189
platforms that we're on, sort of shifting
and reevaluating.

00:00:24.189 --> 00:00:28.130
And very often we'll consider a change and
then we'll, we'll end up not doing anything

00:00:28.130 --> 00:00:32.550
because the consensus ends up being keep doing
things the way that you're doing what you're

00:00:32.550 --> 00:00:37.390
doing is working at least to some degree,
don't, uh, fix something that's not broken.

00:00:37.390 --> 00:00:41.980
But we've in the past also sometimes made
good changes to the show, which from my perspective

00:00:41.980 --> 00:00:44.260
have improved it and the show has continued
to grow.

00:00:44.260 --> 00:00:48.470
So in a sense they weren't bad decisions,
at least not obviously so.

00:00:48.470 --> 00:00:53.579
So remember that for every idea I'm about
to suggest to you, the constraint we have

00:00:53.579 --> 00:00:57.719
is that we're doing a daily TV and radio show
that's an hour long.

00:00:57.719 --> 00:01:03.160
So we're working within that timeframe of
an hour in order for the show to fit in to

00:01:03.160 --> 00:01:07.630
the format of the nearly 200 TV and radio
affiliates that we have.

00:01:07.630 --> 00:01:11.650
That's the show that gets chopped up into
pieces for youtube and are turned into our

00:01:11.650 --> 00:01:13.160
daily audio podcast.

00:01:13.160 --> 00:01:14.900
So don't freak out.

00:01:14.900 --> 00:01:16.360
All of these are just ideas.

00:01:16.360 --> 00:01:20.590
They're based on things I've heard from the
audience most frequently.

00:01:20.590 --> 00:01:23.700
But none of these are changes we're necessarily
making.

00:01:23.700 --> 00:01:28.610
These are just ideas that I will open the
door to hear from you about number one, a

00:01:28.610 --> 00:01:30.640
lot of interview related ideas.

00:01:30.640 --> 00:01:34.200
Some people don't like the interviews on the
show, they just want to hear commentary.

00:01:34.200 --> 00:01:36.650
There's no rule that says we have to keep
doing interviews.

00:01:36.650 --> 00:01:39.260
We've done something like 1500 interviews
on the show.

00:01:39.260 --> 00:01:42.310
Uh, booking interviews is time intensive.

00:01:42.310 --> 00:01:45.690
We could eliminate interviews altogether and
we could add stories.

00:01:45.690 --> 00:01:49.190
So instead of doing six stories per show,
we could get rid of interviews and do eight

00:01:49.190 --> 00:01:50.790
stories per show.

00:01:50.790 --> 00:01:56.020
We could cut the interviews but not add any
stories, meaning we'll still do six stories,

00:01:56.020 --> 00:01:59.570
but we can devote a little more time to each
of those six stories.

00:01:59.570 --> 00:02:05.110
We could cut interviews and cut the number
of stories to only four, which would mean

00:02:05.110 --> 00:02:08.950
the show would become, instead of sort of
like a summary of what happened in the last

00:02:08.950 --> 00:02:13.640
24 hours or over the weekend, we would choose
four stories and cover each story for about

00:02:13.640 --> 00:02:14.710
15 minutes.

00:02:14.710 --> 00:02:17.370
But we would only be covering four things
per day that would say that would change the

00:02:17.370 --> 00:02:18.950
nature of the show.

00:02:18.950 --> 00:02:23.490
We could extend the interviews, make them
longer, but cut them to only a couple of times

00:02:23.490 --> 00:02:24.490
a week.

00:02:24.490 --> 00:02:29.520
So instead of for 13 to 15 minute interviews
per week, we would do just a couple, but they

00:02:29.520 --> 00:02:31.190
could be a half hour long.

00:02:31.190 --> 00:02:33.160
Instead of just 13 to 15 minutes.

00:02:33.160 --> 00:02:37.190
We could do one interview per week and it
would be the entire show.

00:02:37.190 --> 00:02:43.700
So imagine that maybe Wednesday the show instead
of being news and analysis is just an hour

00:02:43.700 --> 00:02:47.690
interview with someone who warrants an hour
of discussion.

00:02:47.690 --> 00:02:50.940
And then the rest of the week would be just
news stories.

00:02:50.940 --> 00:02:52.570
Those are some ideas.

00:02:52.570 --> 00:02:53.570
Live calls.

00:02:53.570 --> 00:02:54.750
Now I know that the live calls are controversial.

00:02:54.750 --> 00:03:00.410
We, we did a poll about live calls previously
and overwhelmingly the audience did want to

00:03:00.410 --> 00:03:03.580
keep live calls even though lots of people
hate them and want them to go.

00:03:03.580 --> 00:03:07.490
So live calls are not on the chopping block
right now, but we could change when and how

00:03:07.490 --> 00:03:08.540
we do live calls.

00:03:08.540 --> 00:03:12.940
So right now we do live calls on the Friday
show and then at the end of Monday through

00:03:12.940 --> 00:03:17.180
Thursdays shows I'll play a voicemail from
the audience and react to it.

00:03:17.180 --> 00:03:22.260
We could instead look at, for example, getting
rid of the voicemail segment, getting rid

00:03:22.260 --> 00:03:28.700
of a half hour of live calls on Friday, and
just do two or three live calls at the end

00:03:28.700 --> 00:03:29.790
of each show.

00:03:29.790 --> 00:03:34.100
So we get rid of voicemails, we do like 10
minutes of live calls at the end of each show.

00:03:34.100 --> 00:03:37.170
But there's no big block of 30 minutes of
calls on Friday.

00:03:37.170 --> 00:03:38.640
That's a possibility.

00:03:38.640 --> 00:03:43.819
Um, there are more logistics for that because
we'd need to open the phone lines every day

00:03:43.819 --> 00:03:47.080
unless we recorded all the calls at once,
which would make some of them may be stale

00:03:47.080 --> 00:03:48.080
and outdated.

00:03:48.080 --> 00:03:52.069
It is more work on our end, but it's an idea
and as many of you know, I'm all about ideas.

00:03:52.069 --> 00:03:56.220
I'm all about big ideas, small ideas, medium
ideas, stale ones, new ones, whatever.

00:03:56.220 --> 00:03:57.700
I'm throwing them out to you.

00:03:57.700 --> 00:04:01.270
So here is how I want to hear from you about
this.

00:04:01.270 --> 00:04:02.810
Only by email.

00:04:02.810 --> 00:04:09.000
There's a reason why it's too easy to just
put up a poll on Twitter or on our website

00:04:09.000 --> 00:04:13.740
or on Youtube and let people vote and just
click something without really thinking about

00:04:13.740 --> 00:04:14.740
it.

00:04:14.740 --> 00:04:18.030
And the thing is that most people often don't
want anything changed.

00:04:18.030 --> 00:04:21.959
But if they're given a list of options, they'll
just pick something and we get sort of cloudy

00:04:21.959 --> 00:04:22.959
data.

00:04:22.959 --> 00:04:27.060
If you actually care enough to want something
changed on the show, whether it's from the

00:04:27.060 --> 00:04:32.720
options I mentioned or something different
altogether, email me through the contact form@davidpacman.com

00:04:32.720 --> 00:04:33.720
okay.

00:04:33.720 --> 00:04:36.150
David pakman.com click on contact.

00:04:36.150 --> 00:04:39.060
Fill out that form and tell me which of these
ideas you like.

00:04:39.060 --> 00:04:41.750
If any, tell me if you want everything to
stay as it is.

00:04:41.750 --> 00:04:44.730
Tell me if there's a change that you would
like that I have not mentioned.

00:04:44.730 --> 00:04:45.730
Okay.

00:04:45.730 --> 00:04:49.730
All of these ideas and others I'm willing
to consider and the advantage of having to

00:04:49.730 --> 00:04:54.830
email me instead of just clicking a poll is
that if you, number one, have an idea I didn't

00:04:54.830 --> 00:04:56.930
mention, we can also include it and consider
it.

00:04:56.930 --> 00:04:58.180
I want those as well.

00:04:58.180 --> 00:05:00.900
Uh, but if you want nothing changed.

00:05:00.900 --> 00:05:04.530
That's also useful to hear because if 80%
of the audience writes in and says, David,

00:05:04.530 --> 00:05:06.580
don't change anything, that's important for
us to hear.

00:05:06.580 --> 00:05:09.480
The whole point here is the show is for you.

00:05:09.480 --> 00:05:12.630
I want the show to be what people want in
terms of the format.

00:05:12.630 --> 00:05:14.300
Obviously I'm going to still pick the guests.

00:05:14.300 --> 00:05:18.389
I'm going to still cover the stories I want
to cover, but as far as the format goes, let

00:05:18.389 --> 00:05:19.389
me know what you think.

00:05:19.389 --> 00:05:24.650
I'll give it like a week or so and then I
will come to you with the results and uh,

00:05:24.650 --> 00:05:25.631
whatever decisions we make about the format
of the show,

